one way to think how stop gradient work:

the prediction of 1536 dstilled emebdding vector is not accurate at first with high mse
yet the prediction yet is trained to make prediction with emebdding+noise
as training proceeds, the mse gets less.
in effect, we are using mse loss as a regularisation to smooth the loss landscape of prediction head (bce loss)
or you can treat emebdding+decreasing noise as augmentation
or you can treat it as : stop gradient method = direct onnex method + "unbias shift"

